# api: optional Core ML export dependencies.
# Installed only when the operator opts in:
#   scripts/macos/install_macos.sh --with-coreml
# or manually: `pip install -r requirements-coreml.txt` (the lockfile compiled
# from this manifest; regenerate with
# `uv pip compile requirements-coreml.in -o requirements-coreml.txt --python-version 3.11 --universal`).
#
# macOS only, and deliberately not a platform marker in requirements.in.
# coremltools publishes wheels for macOS and manylinux and none for Windows,
# so on Windows pip falls back to the sdist and builds a pure-Python package
# with the C++ extensions missing. That install imports, converts, and then
# fails at the two things that matter: mlprogram serialisation needs
# BlobWriter from libmilstoragepython, and predict() needs libcoremlpython.
# Measured on this project's sibling on 2026-08-19 -- a half-working
# coremltools on PATH is worse than none, because the export looks available
# and produces an artifact nobody can check against the bank.
#
# The upper bound tracks what coremltools declares it has been tested against
# (_TORCH_MAX_VERSION), not what happens to import. Conversion runs the torch
# frontend, so a torch far ahead of that is exactly where silent breakage
# lives.
coremltools>=9.0
